<title>GREECE: EXPIRIES OF GREEK GOVT DEBT SECURITIES IN JULY.</title>
<headline>EXPIRIES OF GREEK GOVT DEBT SECURITIES IN JULY.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is information on the</p>
<p>expiries of Greece's drachma and foreign currency-linked and</p>
<p>denominated government debt in July.</p>
<p>    ISSUE DATE	  AMOUNT RAISED	   COUPON</p>
<p>  July  1, 1996  173 bln drachmas	     13.30%</p>
<p>  JUly 10, 1990   60 bln yen		     7.4%</p>
<p>  July 15, 1994    7,698,000 mark-linked     6.95%</p>
<p>  July 17, 1996  155 bln drachmas	     13.0%  (12-m T-bill)</p>
<p>  July 28, 1994   50 bln yen		     4.5%</p>
<p>  July 30, 1996  258 bln drachmas	     12.80% (12-m T-bill)</p>
<p>  July 31, 1992   97 bln drachmas		12-mth T-bill</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
